{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"The promise diagnostics resolve the upstream question and refute the leading explanation. In convergence round 3 node 4 received four Promises carrying its ballot n=2: nodes 1, 2 and 5 each reported accept round 1, accepted index 37 and a log_sync containing the StopSign, while node 3 reported accept round 0 and accepted 0 without a StopSign. Because PromiseMetaData orders by accept round and then accepted index, the greatest promise is one of the StopSign-bearing ones, so the single max_promise_sync merge did carry the StopSign, and node 4's accepted index rose from 0 to 37 in that same round. The max-merge hazard is therefore not the cause of this run: leader 4 did acquire the StopSign, but only in round 3, after it had already sent node 3 the AcceptSync that left node 3 at accepted 37 with decided 0. The two later Decides carry counters 2 and 3, the immediate successors of that AcceptSync, so they are sequence-expected and clamp decided to 37, no PrepareReq is sent, and no AcceptStopSign ever reaches node 3. The update records the promise evidence as a new fact, refutes the max-merge attribution for run 13 in the question's knowledge, keeps the reported-index decision mechanism since node 4 ended accepted 37 with decided 38, and restates the interpretation with one remaining open point: since the StopSign holders also reported accepted 37, the receipt cannot tell whether node 3's position 37 is the StopSign or a later position is missing. The progress loss itself remains established and agreement unaffected. No execution is requested.\"}"}}
